# PlatformIO build output. Hundreds of megabytes: toolchains, framework
# packages and object files, all reproducible from platformio.ini.
.pio/

# The repo-root virtualenv the tools need (xxhash, cryptography).
.venv/

# Serial captures and build logs from tools/devrun.sh and friends.
*.log

# Host test binaries land in $TMPDIR, but not if TMPDIR is unset and someone
# edits a runner to write here instead.
lc_test_*

.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deliberately NOT ignored, though all of it is generated:
#
#   src/checkpoint.h            the trust root, and the only thing believed
#                               a priori. It has to be reviewed in a diff.
#   src/checkpoint_precomp.c    1.4 MB of point tables derived from those keys.
#                               Large, but it must travel with checkpoint.h or
#                               the two fall out of step - main.cpp #errors if
#                               they disagree on set_id, and regenerating it
#                               needs the venv. A clone should build as-is.
#   test/fixtures/              real mainnet data the host tests assert against.
#                               Regenerating needs network, and fresh captures
#                               would silently change what the tests prove.
#
# The rule: if a checkout cannot build or cannot run its tests without it, it
# is committed, however generated it looks.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
